---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import '../styles/legal.css';
import { site, pending } from '../data/site';
import { withBase } from '../utils/url';
---

<Base
  title="Tax advice notice"
  description="What this website is, what it isn't, and where the line sits between reading a page here and being a client of NTA, Inc."
  chrome="legal"
  legalSibling={{ label: 'Site policies', href: '/site-policies' }}
>
  <div class="container legal">
    <h1 class="h1 legal__title">Tax advice notice</h1>
    {/* Page opener: the one horizontal gold rule on this page. */}
    <hr class="gold-rule legal__rule" />
    <p class="lead measure-64 legal__intro">
      What this website is, what it isn't, and where the line sits between reading a page here and
      being a client.
    </p>
    <p class="label legal__effective">EFFECTIVE {pending.legalEffectiveDate}</p>
    <p class="confirm-note measure-64 legal__draft">
      Draft for your review. I am not a lawyer and this text has not been reviewed by one — the
      bracketed notes mark what needs your confirmation before this page goes live.
    </p>

    <div class="legal__body">
      <section>
        <h2 class="h2 legal__h2">Nothing here is advice for your situation</h2>
        <p class="legal__p">
          The pages on this site describe the work I do in general terms. General is the operative
          word: a sentence that is true for most filers may be exactly wrong for you, and the useful
          answer almost always depends on facts that aren't on a website.
        </p>
        <p class="legal__p">
          Do not act, or decline to act, on the basis of anything you read here. Ask me, or ask
          another qualified professional, about your own circumstances first.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="h2 legal__h2">You become a client when we sign, not before</h2>
        <p class="legal__p">
          Sending an inquiry does not create a professional relationship. Neither does a phone call,
          an email exchange, or my answering a question at no charge. An engagement begins when there
          is a written engagement letter naming the work, the period, and the fee, signed by both of
          us.
        </p>
        <p class="legal__p">
          Until then I have no duty to act on a deadline you are facing, and you should not assume a
          filing is being handled.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="h2 legal__h2">Don't send sensitive information</h2>
        <p class="legal__p">
          The inquiry form and ordinary email are not secure channels. Please keep Social Security
          and taxpayer ID numbers, bank and brokerage account numbers, and copies of returns out of a
          first message. A description is enough — "three years unfiled, sole proprietor, Illinois"
          tells me what I need.
        </p>
        <p class="legal__p">
          Once we're working together, I'll tell you how to send documents properly.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="h2 legal__h2">Links to other sites</h2>
        <p class="legal__p">
          Where this site links to the IRS, FINRA, a state revenue department, or any other outside
          source, it is for convenience. I don't control those pages, I'm not responsible for what
          they say, and a link is not an endorsement.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="h2 legal__h2">Past results are not a promise</h2>
        <p class="legal__p">
          Descriptions of past engagements — an examination resolved, a filing brought current, a net
          capital issue cleared — describe what happened in those matters. Facts differ, examiners
          differ, and the law changes. Nothing here should be read as a prediction about your
          outcome.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="h2 legal__h2">Written advice and Circular 230</h2>
        <p class="legal__p">
          Practice before the IRS is governed by Treasury Department Circular 230. Any written advice
          I give a client is prepared for that client's specific facts, and it isn't intended for
          anyone else to rely on or to use to avoid penalties.
        </p>
        <p class="confirm-note">
          [CONFIRM] Whether you want the formal Circular 230 wording your engagement letters already
          use, so the site and the letters read the same. If you send it to me I'll drop it in
          verbatim.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="h2 legal__h2">Who is behind this site</h2>
        <p class="legal__p">
          {site.name} — {site.principalName}, Certified Public Accountant since 1983. Chicago area,
          plus remote clients nationwide.
        </p>
        <p class="confirm-note">
          [CONFIRM] Licensure jurisdiction ({pending.licensureJurisdictionShort}), and whether a PTIN
          should be displayed here.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="legal__questions">
        <h2 class="h2 legal__h2 legal__h2--sm">Questions about any of this</h2>
        <p class="legal__p">
          Call <a href={site.phoneHref}>{site.phone}</a> or write to
          <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>. See also
          <a href={withBase('/site-policies')}>site policies</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
